{"step_index":5752,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T20:18:44Z","thinking":"Deterministic auto-matches are consistent across the runs. The \"السلام شبين,\" \"جملة العمروووو,\" \"المكرومي,\" and \"الهضبة\" examples all produce identical results. This suggests a stable, predictable behavior for these specific patterns.\n\n\nThe deterministic engine exhibits consistent behavior, while variance arises from the local LLM's handling of ambiguous entries. Specifically, the LLM incorrectly matched \"Neocarbon\" with \"Eucarbon\" in one case and suggested \"Controloc\" as a match for \"Protiloc\" (both are pantoprazole) in another, differing from previous runs. These discrepancies highlight the LLM's susceptibility to OCR errors or slight variations in its output, potentially due to non-deterministic factors.\n\n\nThe agent identified an inconsistency: the LLM accepted `'ديكابرينو 200 مجم 2 امبول'` as a match for `'ديكابرين أقراص'` in one run despite the different forms (ampoule vs. tablet). The agent notes reasonable matches like `'توب جنج ادفانس 30 كبسولة'` with `'توب جينج كبسول'`.\n\nSeveral cases involving likely OCR errors were also detected: `'زنكترون 30 كبسولة'` matched with `'زنكتون اقراص'`, `'كارنيفيتا ادفانس للرجال'` with `'كارنتينا ادفانس رجال'`, and `'زوكوزيت 20/10 مجم اقراص'` with `'زكوجينت 20/10 مجم قرص'`.\n\nThe LLM incorrectly matched \"Zithromax\" (in a run) with its Egyptian alternative \"Zithron,\" indicating potential ambiguity handling issues. This was accepted in a past run, but rejected in a later run.\n\n\nThe LLM demonstrates fluctuating behavior in matching drug entries, exemplified by inconsistent decisions on `'سيديتيل'`, `'اورامكس'`, `'فاستر جيل'`, and `'سيديرال بمبي'`.  The agent notes the LLM now directly accepted `'ديكابرينو أمبول'` and `'نيوكاربون'` as matches, removing them from the \"needs review\" list, leading to changes in the count of items in PROC-012. Deterministic rules, however, rema